== a select menu variable must be a plain name ==
1:8: error: Bad select loop variable, '$menu' is not a plain name.
     1 |  select $menu in a b c; do break; done
       |         ^~~~~
note: Drop the '$' and any quotes.
1:24: error: 'do' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select $menu in a b c; do break; done
       |                         ^~
1:34: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select $menu in a b c; do break; done
       |                                   ^~~~
rc=1
== a quoted select menu variable is rejected the same way ==
1:8: error: Bad select loop variable, 'menu' is not a plain name.
     1 |  select "menu" in a b c; do break; done
       |         ^~~~~~
note: Drop the '$' and any quotes.
1:25: error: 'do' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select "menu" in a b c; do break; done
       |                          ^~
1:35: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select "menu" in a b c; do break; done
       |                                    ^~~~
rc=1
== a select menu variable that is not an identifier is rejected ==
1:8: error: Bad select loop variable, '9bad' is not a plain name.
     1 |  select 9bad in a b c; do break; done
       |         ^~~~
note: Drop the '$' and any quotes.
1:23: error: 'do' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select 9bad in a b c; do break; done
       |                        ^~
1:33: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select 9bad in a b c; do break; done
       |                                  ^~~~
rc=1
== a plain select menu variable is accepted ==
1) a
2) b
#? picked a
rc=0
== select is not a keyword outside bash mood ==
1:24: error: 'do' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select $menu in a b c; do break; done
       |                         ^~
1:34: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
     1 |  select $menu in a b c; do break; done
       |                                   ^~~~
rc=1
== a select menu word is checked against the sh shebang ==
2:16: warning: The `$"..."` quoting form is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3004)
     2 |  select menu in item=$"select locale"; do break; done
       |                 ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use ordinary double quotes under a `sh` shebang.
rc=0
